# Project standards

This repository is the only home for BestHR Investigations source code. Keep every page, style, script, asset, and document here.

- Prefer standard HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Do not add a framework, package, library, or build tool unless it is necessary and approved.
- Do not add a backend, database, CMS, or authentication without explicit approval.
- Do not add an external service, account, or piece of infrastructure without explicit approval.
- Explain an architectural change, and wait for approval, before implementing it.
- Document every dependency and every piece of infrastructure in `docs/` before it is used.
- Never hardcode credentials, API keys, tokens, or secrets. Do not commit them.
- Do not remove existing functionality without explicit approval.
- Keep code organized, readable, and portable so a person can maintain it in any text editor without Cursor or other AI tools.
- Do not install packages or generate website pages as part of setup work unless that work was explicitly requested.

```html
<!-- Bad: hidden service and a secret in source -->
<script src="https://example-cdn.example/widget.js"></script>
<script>const apiKey = "sk_live_...";</script>

<!-- Good: local file, no secret, purpose is obvious -->
<script src="/src/js/navigation.js"></script>
```
